## Context

Source monitoring must record what was attempted and what succeeded, while producing candidates for existing monthly-edition ticket 0728.

Design: `docs/jetp-backend-design.md`, revision 5. Plan: `docs/jetp-backend-implementation-plan.md`. Parent: 0760 (except the tracker itself, which belongs to 0725/#1333). Proposed work; no implementation authorized by filing.

## First test

A frozen sweep contains unchanged, revised, blocked and deferred targets. Every target has a result; only successful coverage advances; a blocked target cannot erase evidence or trigger publication.

## Actions

Implement reviewed watch policies, immutable source revisions, frozen sweep targets/checks/discoveries, schedule derivation and idempotent acquisition links. Distinguish discovery-page and document targets. Produce changes since principal reports with claim-specific origin/dependency assessments, not automatic factual promotion. Preserve late reports/corrections and editorial impact queues; hand results to 0728.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Every frozen target has a check or explicit deferral
- [ ] Failed/repeated checks preserve attempts and successful-coverage semantics
- [ ] Changed metadata cannot rewrite older sweeps or cutoff views
- [ ] Same discovery retains identity with multiple discovery links
- [ ] Candidate change report identifies affected claims and never publishes unattended

## Validation and recovery

Start implementation with the failing fixture. Run make check-fast and make lint; run the full make check for pipeline-surface diffs under AGENTS.md. Run the existing browser exercise for output/renderer changes. Cite exact fixture IDs and input/output commits in the PR. Preserve last accepted static output; candidate failure must not change canonical ownership or publish partial files. No deployment, estimator or PyPSA work is included in this ticket.

